<h1>Preferences - CSV/ASCII File Export</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>CSV/ASCII File Export settings are used for formatting the export of the following data:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">In normal mode:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul type="circle" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p">
<p>Points and polylines in ASC file - <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>File &gt; Export: ASCII Points (*.asc)</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p>Entities information in CSV file - <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>File &gt; Export: CSV File (*.csv)</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet" value="1">
<p class="bullet">In Inspection mode:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul type="disc" class="whs4">
<li style="list-style:circle;" type="circle" class="kadov-p">
<p>Labels information in CSV file - <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>File &gt; Export Labels</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:circle;" type="circle" class="kadov-p">
<p>Inspection points in CSV file - <span style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>File &gt; Export 3D Points</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="whs6"><img src="Images/CSV_export_settings.gif" width="593px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head">Separator group</p>
<p class="bullet">Sets the separator character:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>System List Separator</b></span> - this separator is a property of Microsoft Windows. In Microsoft Windows XP you can find and change it if you open <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Control Panel</i></span> and double-click on <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Regional and Language Settings</i></span> applet. Then select <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Regional Options</i></span> tab and press on <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Customise</i></span> button. In the <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Customise Regional Options</i></span> dialog, that will appear, select <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Numbers</i></span> tab and find <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>List Separator</i></span> listbox. There is a predefined list separator for each language supported by the operating system.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Comma</b></span> (,).</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tab</b></span> - tabulation.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Semicolon</b></span> (;).</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Space</b></span>.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Other</b></span> - user defined character.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Text qualifier</b></span> (none, quote (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span>), or double quotes (<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>"</b></span>)) - used for enclosing text so characters that are selected for separators but within the text will not be treated as separators.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Digits format group</p>
<p><span style="font-size:10pt; color:#000000;"><font size="2" color="black" style="font-size:10.000000pt;">Sets the representation of the numbers in the CSV file:</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Left of decimal</b></span> - number of digits (including leading zeros if enabled) left of decimal point. Significant digits are not limited by this parameter.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Right of decimal</b></span> - number of digits right of decimal point.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Display leading zeros</b></span> - sets whether to display or not leading zeros if the number of significant digits is less than the number set for 'Left of decimal' parameter.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Always display sign</b></span> - sets whether to display or not the plus sign.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Preview</b></span> - shows the representation of the numbers according to the settings in this group.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Angle display group</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Decimal format</b></span> - sets whether to display or not the degrees in decimal or in degree/minute/second format (XXdXXmXXs) (1min = 1/60deg, 1sec = 1/3600deg) and the grads in decimal or in grad/centigrade/deci-milligrad format (XXgXXcXXcc) (1c = 1/100grad, 1cc = 1/10000grad). The unit for angle display can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>/Preferences/Units</i></span>.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Round slot length group</p>
<p class="bullet">Sets the output for round slot length (this setting is applicable only for CSV export of entities information):</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Full length</b></span> This is the default length for round slots in KUBE. It is calculated by the distance between the two semicircles of the slot + 2*radius.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Center to center</b></span> This is the distance between the centres of the two semicircles of the slot.</p>
